WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.630
In 2000, China imported about
10.4 million tonnes of soybeans.

2
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:10.390
By 2023, it was 103.4 million tonnes.

3
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.390
About ten times as much.

4
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:18.190
In 2025, nearly 3 in 4 came from
Brazil, on another continent.

5
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.750
So why does what people eat in
China matter to land in Brazil?

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.170
Is it more tofu?

7
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.730
Soy for car fuel?

8
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.950
Or soils in China that
cannot grow soybeans?

9
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.430
In this mission, you'll measure
the land that feeds the world,

10
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.610
and why enough food still
leaves people hungry.

11
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:39.210
Then you'll map a spatial
interaction across two continents,

12
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.070
and weigh who gains and who pays.

13
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.390
Your mission: explain why what people
eat in China matters to land in Brazil.
